From 9013a81414ceffc1edbae6c8c36cc8f63d86af07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:03:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(wash): trust the system certificate store for OCI
 commands

`wash oci push`/`pull` and `wash inspect` only trusted the compiled-in
webpki roots plus `--ca-path` bundles, so a registry behind a private CA
failed with `UnknownIssuer` even when the CA was in the OS trust store or
SSL_CERT_FILE / SSL_CERT_DIR, and the error gave no hint about the flag.

wash-runtime gains an opt-in `set_trust_native_roots` that adds the
platform's native roots (loaded once, filtered to certificates webpki
accepts) to every OCI client. It stays off by default, so a host keeps its
reproducible compiled-in trust; the CLI turns it on. `--ca-path` is
unchanged. An UnknownIssuer failure now points at `--ca-path`.

Closes #5607
---
